Package: aspersions
Title: Cast Shade and Sight Lines on Terrain
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: 
    person("Michael", "Sumner", , "mdsumner@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Viewsheds and cast shadows for terrain. Viewsheds are exact,
    computed as an object-space visibility map on the terrain as triangles:
    the visible part of every triangle seen from a point, as polygons, with
    the skyline from that point as a by-product. Cast shadows for a sun
    position use one directional sweep over the grid, with an optional
    coarse far field for distant ridges and earth curvature. Implemented in
    Rust (the 'osvm' crate, vendored) via 'extendr'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/hypertidy/aspersions
BugReports: https://github.com/hypertidy/aspersions/issues
